    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0356" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1334.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-20T15:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dominican Government to-day requests that the Department take some action to
                    prevent the smuggling of arms and ammunition into Monte Cristi by the Haitian
                    gunboat which scarcely takes the trouble to conceal its operations. This conduct
                    on the part of the Haitian Government is conducive to prolonged revolutionary
                    activities. Receivership has reports indicating that the Haitian gunboat is
                    operating from Monte Cristi to some point along the border and that the
                    Receivership forces are not strong enough to prevent the Haitian gunboat from
                    smuggling and interfering with the United States rights under the Treaty of
                    1907. If the Haitian Government cannot be brought to realize its obligations it
                    is likely that the Dominican Government will declare war against Haiti.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
